 "content": {
  "subject": "Power Systems",
  "topic": "Corona Phenomenon in Transmission Lines",
  "difficulty": "Easy",
  "hook": "Why do high voltage lines hiss and glow in the dark?",
  "question": "Which modification will increase the critical disruptive voltage and effectively reduce corona loss on an overhead line?",
  "options": [
   "Increasing conductor spacing",
   "Decreasing conductor radius",
   "Operating under stormy weather",
   "Using rough stranded conductors"
  ],
  "correctIndex": 0,
  "answerLine": "Increasing conductor spacing increases the critical disruptive voltage.",
  "explanation": [
   "Critical disruptive voltage is the minimum phase voltage where air breakdown begins around a conductor.",
   "The standard expression is Vd equals m naught g naught delta r natural log of d over r.",
   "Here d represents the spacing between line conductors, while r is the overall conductor radius.",
   "Increasing spacing d directly raises the ratio d over r inside that natural logarithm term."
  ],
  "funFact": "Corona discharge produces ozone gas and a faint violet glow known historically to sailors as Saint Elmo's fire.",
  "outro": "Mastering corona formulas is essential for AE and JE exams. Follow for more daily electrical practice!",
